{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A CSP header without a nonce or hash blocks every inline script and onclick handler on your site, not just an attacker's — move code to external files, or explicitly allowlist the inline script you actually own.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Never fix a CSP violation by adding 'unsafe-inline' — that disables the protection sitewide. Use a per-response nonce on both the policy and the script tag instead.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Ship new policies as Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only first to find every inline dependency before enforcing, and remember style-src gates inline styles the same way script-src gates inline script.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
